From 76fb424438760aad34b0b650dcaa02b344ad9e8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:54:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] Media: say where a picture's stereo mode comes from

StereoMode now names every arrangement a file or stream may give: the
values of Matroska's StereoMode (RFC 9559, section 5.1.4.1.28.3, Table 5)
and the frame packing SEI's arrangements (H.264 and H.265, Table D-8):
side by side, top and bottom, checkerboard, rows, columns, frame
sequence, each with either eye first, and the two anaglyph pairs.

StereoSource tells where a picture's mode comes from, in the order the
edition reads them: the stream's frame packing SEI, the container's mark
(with the size of one view, Matroska's DisplayWidth and DisplayHeight,
RFC 9559 section 18.10, or without it), the user's choice, a WebXR
session. Whether the size of a view is known decides whether the views
are taken for half or full size.

VideoInfo carries both from the demuxer, and DMABuf surfaces carry both
to the compositor in their descriptor.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
